 "script": [
  "If you live in tornado country, the safest room you can own is buried under your backyard.",
  "But the wind up top can throw a car, so you dig a pit eight feet down.",
  "But dirt walls cave in, so you pour a concrete floor and three thick walls.",
  "This is the shell.",
  "But a roof is the first thing a tornado rips off, so you cap it with a concrete lid full of steel bars.",
  "But now there's no way in, so you add stairs and a steel door.",
  "But a sealed box runs out of fresh air, so you add two air vents.",
  "But rain falls straight down the vents, so you bend their tops into hooks.",
  "This is called a gooseneck vent.",
  "But water still seeps through the ground, so you add a drain and a little pump.",
  "But when the power dies it's pitch black, so you hang a battery lantern.",
  "But you can't hear the warnings down here, so you add a weather radio.",
  "But you might be stuck for hours, so you bolt benches to the walls and stack water.",
  "Fun fact: safe room doors are tested by firing a fifteen pound two by four at them at one hundred miles an hour.",
  "Now the sirens go, the family runs down the stairs, the door slams shut, and the storm passes right over the top.",
  "And that's how a backyard became the safest room in town."
 ],
